From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000185 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: bind P32 operation to target

Require the CPU8 operation for target 8 and the CPU9 operation for target 9
at both publication and every later guard. A mismatched operation/CPU pair is
stale identity and must not enter the rollback side channel.

This experiment-only change has no certifying sign-off and is not
submission-ready.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c
@@ -205,4 +205,6 @@ mt6797_a72_p32_target_locked(unsigned int cpu)
 		(transaction->identity.operation ==
 		 ARM64_LATE_CPU_STARTUP_OP_CPU8_UP ||
 		 transaction->identity.operation ==
 		 ARM64_LATE_CPU_STARTUP_OP_CPU9_UP) &&
+		transaction->identity.operation == (cpu == 8 ?
+		 ARM64_LATE_CPU_STARTUP_OP_CPU8_UP : ARM64_LATE_CPU_STARTUP_OP_CPU9_UP) &&
 		transaction->identity.target_cpu == cpu &&
@@ -237,4 +239,6 @@ int mt6797_a72_membership_publish_p32(unsigned int cpu,
 	    (transaction->identity.operation !=
 		 ARM64_LATE_CPU_STARTUP_OP_CPU8_UP &&
 	     transaction->identity.operation !=
 		 ARM64_LATE_CPU_STARTUP_OP_CPU9_UP) ||
+	    transaction->identity.operation != (cpu == 8 ?
+		 ARM64_LATE_CPU_STARTUP_OP_CPU8_UP : ARM64_LATE_CPU_STARTUP_OP_CPU9_UP) ||
 	    transaction->identity.generation == 0 ||
